R-PA13 R-PA5 R-PA6 R-DI12 R-EC14 R-DI2 R-OUT2 (slice 070, a base that no release of the group has): 3 runs on one project. p1 has json 2.2.0 in the header (it is in the cache) and a patch whose `base` is the hash of a json 2.1.5 that is not in the cache and that no release of the list has. The release list of acme/json (the fake HTTP, 3 releases: 2.1.0, 2.2.0, 2.3.0) is not in the index dir yet. `tln install` with no names applies the patch to the header release (R-PA6), so it needs the base for the diff (R-PA5).
Run 1 (`install --offline`): `packages/<base>` is missing (one `list_dirs` of it), so Talon looks for the base in the release list of the group. With `--offline` and no cached page there is no list: exit 15, the text of R-DI12 for a missing page (`Github.no_page_failure`). Run 2 (`install`): the list is requested (2 pages of the cache are written) and no release of the group (acme/json, series 2) has the hash: exit 14 (kind `frozen`), the text names the base, the alias and the 2 fixes of R-PA5 (`Patched.base_missing`). Nothing is written but the index pages: no copy, no `talon.toml`, no header, no temp dir. Run 3 (`install --offline`): the same exit 14 from the cached pages, and stderr has the line `index: cached at <time>` (R-DI12). The hash of a release of another group or repository is no release of the group (L0 `PatchedTest`). A base that a release has is a download (R-PA13, question Q1 of the slice file): no run.
